Z||000000||Kage86GT4SP||07-08-2000||03:31 AM||||OK, I'm driving down the freeway, and my SES light comes on.  There's no change in the engine performance; no noticeable difference in the guages.  <P>The engine has to be warm... and so far, it only happens at freeway speed.<P>I checked the EGR, and it seems to be functional.<P>Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR>86 SE 2.8 4 spd (5spd in the garage, and turbo on the shelf) <P>86 Trans Am w/89 383 vette stroker/TPI/700R4/MSD6A/Blaster/Accel/SLP Stainless Headers/Edelbrock Cat Back. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||ponya||07-08-2000||06:43 AM||||Had a similar problem. Light only came on at cruising speed. Turned out to be a cracked vacumn line that ran underneath the plenum to the egr solenoid. A lot of heat and old vacumn lines. Changed the hose and its been fine since. Hope that helps,    Bob||||reg||1
